<section class="block-section reflect">
  <span class="section-tag">Reflect</span>
  <h2>Before next class</h2>
  <p class="sub">Block 5 is the AI source and the documentation, and it needs your two traditional sources already done. This is the one substantial piece of homework in Unit 0.</p>
  <p class="sub">Graded formative, same as your Lovelock OPVL. You bring it to Block 5.</p>
  <div class="submission-callout">
    <div class="label">OPVL your two traditional sources</div>
    <p>Finish the OPVL on your <strong>traditional reputable source</strong> and complete one on your <strong>potentially weaker source</strong>. Four to eight sentences each, on the structured template.</p>
    <p>Two things to hold on to while you write:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The <strong>Limitation</strong> must be specific to that source. "Could be biased" is not a Limitation, it is a shrug. Name what this particular source cannot tell you and why.</li>
      <li>"Weaker" does not mean wrong. It means different Origin, Purpose, Value, and Limitations. If your weaker source turns out to be right about something, that is worth writing down.</li>
    </ul>
    {% set submit = { id: "u0-b4-hw", text: "Submit via Google Classroom" } %}{% include "partials/submit-link.njk" %}
  </div>
  <p class="rubric-meta">If you cannot find a second source you are happy with, bring the search you tried and where it dead-ended. That is a real research problem and Block 5 opens with them. Coming in empty-handed with no account of why is the only version of this that does not work.</p>
</section>
